      "mergeID": "67d839bf19624b1eaf42ae66",
      "mergedPostDetails": "It seems like an oversight that drones are able to influence pickups / rigidbodies in worlds. This is not the case for prints, so it shouldn't be the case for drones.\n\nThis is a huge problem for worlds that use rigidbodies under the assumption that no outside influence can disturb them.\n\n(I've attached a gif of this occurring)",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1601] Drones should not influence pickups / rigidbodies in worlds",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "67d21d9854af842b7d229388",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I actually think this isn’t a bad thing. Being able to knock things over is fun :)\n\nWorlds can disable drones if they rely on player only physics interaction. Or maybe a tick box in the world settings for drone interaction would be nice.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
